basic_verification: TP
basic_verification_notes: |
  Crash reproduces consistently under ASan+UBSan through the
  vp9_encoder_svc_layer_config_fuzzer harness (debug build). Top UBSan
  frame is saturate_cast_double_to_int at vpx_dsp_common.h:89, called
  from vp9_update_buffer_level_svc_preencode (vp9_ratectrl.c:295).
  Harness re-audit against the crash path found NO P1 / P2 / P3 / P4
  violations: bitrate ladders are monotonic, ts_periodicity is a
  multiple of ts_number_layers, g_w/g_h are even, API order matches
  examples/vp9_spatial_svc_encoder.c. The crash site is the real
  libvpx defect — lc->framerate is left at 0.0 for (sl, tl) slots
  where sl >= 1 because vp9_update_layer_context_change_config's
  NOLAYERING else-branch only initializes indices 0..number_temporal_layers-1.
binary_reproduction: TP
binary_reproduction_method: repro_app
binary_reproduction_tool: repro_vp9_svc_layer_config
binary_reproduction_notes: |
  Path B. Minimal public-API repro program using only
  vpx/vp8cx.h + vpx/vpx_encoder.h + vpx/vpx_image.h. Built against a
  production-equivalent libvpx (NO --enable-debug) with
  -fsanitize=address,undefined. UBSan fires at
  vpx_dsp_common.h:89:10 via vpx_codec_encode ->
  vp9_get_compressed_data -> vp9_rc_get_svc_params ->
  vp9_update_buffer_level_svc_preencode. Same signature as harness.
  The debug-only assert(ctx->pending_frame_count) at
  vp9_cx_iface.c:1282 is absent (correctly elided by NDEBUG), so the
  UBSan diagnostic is the reportable defect.
root_cause_summary: |
  (int)NaN at vpx_dsp/vpx_dsp_common.h:89 is undefined behavior
  (C11 6.3.1.4). Triggered when vp9_update_buffer_level_svc_preencode
  indexes a per-layer LAYER_CONTEXT whose lc->framerate is still 0.0
  because neither vp9_init_layer_context nor the NOLAYERING branch of
  vp9_update_layer_context_change_config covers all (sl, tl) slots.
proxy_check_release_build: |
  NDEBUG release build with ASan ONLY (no UBSan) ran cleanly on the
  same input: no crash, no ASan error, exit 0. The production
  consequence is SILENT rate-control state corruption
  (implementation-defined integer in lrc->bits_off_target /
  lrc->buffer_level), not a crash / OOB / UAF. Severity capped at
  integrity:low, availability:low accordingly. UBSan-only abort on
  fuzz-tooling builds.
ready_for_upstream: true
classification: keep_with_severity_caveat
caveats: |
  libvpx upstream tends to treat encoder-config-driven NaN->int UBSan
  findings as P3 fuzz-tooling noise unless paired with a visible
  production-build crash. Release-build proxy here runs clean; the
  defect is real but user-visible impact is silent rate-control
  corruption, not a crash. Recommend filing as code-quality /
  defense-in-depth with CVSS:3.1 medium (6.1) but setting expectations
  that upstream may downgrade to low / wontfix.
notes: Verified 2026-04-23 via chrome-verify-crash SOP end-to-end.
